25,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"It seems our external dependencies are risky. Supplier windows for some tech slip easily, and winter roads are unreliable north of the river.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"The outer wards are struggling. Bus links are gone, but old outreach data shows those areas have huge demand if we go to them.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,George,,"The funding is tricky. Grants only cover the first year of sessions, and vehicle costs are overrunning while equipment funds are underused.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,May,,"History repeats itself. A digitisation project failed years ago, but partner-run groups from that same era are still thriving today.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"We have skilled volunteers for repairs, but we lack staff on the payroll who are trained to supervise outside facilitators.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, if the roads close, would a mobile service even be able to reach those outer wards in winter?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Ryuji, that's a worry, but the community halls there stay open. Maybe we just need to be smarter about the timing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,George,,"@Ryuji, if you're seeing delivery slips, we should avoid any project that relies on a strict hardware rollout timeline.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, if we can't supervise facilitators, then any program relying on outside partners might be a liability.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, exactly. I'm worried we're adding work without checking if we have the actual skills to manage it.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@George, you mentioned vehicle costs are overrunning. That makes me very cautious about any proposal involving a fleet.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@George, but if the demand is that high in the outer wards, isn't it worth the cost?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,George,,"@Yumi, only if the funding is sustainable. A one-year grant won't fix a permanent transport gap.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,May,,"@Yumi, remember that partner-run groups survived without us. Maybe the solution isn't us driving there, but supporting them.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree with May. If we don't have the supervisors, a complex new managed service will just overwhelm the staff.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,We need something stable and independent of volatile suppliers or weather.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Yumi,,But we can't ignore the people who have no bus link.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,George,,We must ensure the second year of funding doesn't collapse the project.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,May,,Let's look for a model that has a proven track record of longevity in this system.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,And something that doesn't require specialized supervision we don't have.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
