50,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The candidates are A: Language Learning Circles, B: Digital Archive Portal, C: Maker Workshop, and D: Mobile Branch Service. I dislike D due to roads and costs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Yumi,,D is the only one that helps the outer wards directly. A could work if we use the community halls.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,George,,"A is risky because of the grant terms; the second year will be a struggle. B uses the endowment for capital, which is safer.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,May,,B failed six years ago. A is similar to the partner groups that actually survived. I prefer A.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"C needs tool certification, and our technician retired. A needs facilitators we can't supervise. B seems the most passive.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, B relies on scanning contractors. I found their delivery windows are unreliable. B might never actually launch.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@May, if A uses partner organizations, does that solve the supervision problem Daisuke mentioned?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""May"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, if the partners run it themselves, like those old groups, it avoids the budget cliff I'm worried about.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,May,,"Exactly, Yumi. If the community takes ownership, it doesn't drain our staff or our budget.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@May, if the partners are truly independent, then my concern about payroll supervision is less relevant.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A seems the most resilient. It doesn't depend on roads, hardware delivery, or heavy vehicle maintenance.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Yumi,,I can support A if it means the outer wards get those conversation groups in their own halls.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,George,,"If it's partner-led, it bypasses the grant-to-budget trap. I can move toward A.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,May,,It's the most logical choice. It's a proven model that leverages community strength.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,It's safer than C and more sustainable than D. I'll vote for A.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for A.,"{""words"":4,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
